<section id="corrections">
<h2>Corrections</h2>
<p>If you think a fact on a review is wrong, email <a href="mailto:support@beverified.org?subject=Correction">support@beverified.org</a> with a source. We check every request and update the review when the source supports the change. Providers can correct facts this way; they can't change a score or a ranking position.</p>
</section>

<section id="changelog">
<h2>What changed</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Nov 10, 2026:</strong> sponsored placements on review pages described under <a href="#advertising">Sponsored placements</a>. They don't change scores, rankings or reviews.</li>
<li><strong>Nov 10, 2026 (KYA 1.0):</strong> added a Know Your Agent rubric for products that verify AI agents acting for customers. KYA scores are separate from overall scores and order only the Know Your Agent ranking. Criteria and weights were published before any provider was scored.</li>
<li><strong>Nov 5, 2026 (v3.1):</strong> separate rubrics for identity verification and KYC and for AML, built around what buyers compare: fraud defense or screening quality, total cost, coverage, platform breadth, integration and track record. Certificates now count under trust instead of a 25% criterion of their own. Sub-scores follow fixed rules and every review shows its breakdown. All 47 identity and AML providers were re-scored on the same day; the average score fell from 4.4 to 3.6, and rankings were re-ordered. Quantexa, Verified, VerifyMy and Paravision keep their previous score and are left out of rankings until category-specific rubrics cover them. Travel Rule providers stay on v3.0.</li>
<li><strong>Oct 19, 2026:</strong> disclosure updated: paid provider links are labelled "Sponsored link"; links to providers that don't pay use rel="nofollow".</li>
<li><strong>Oct 18, 2026:</strong> rewritten to describe how reviews are actually built today: public evidence labelled by source, hands-on testing marked separately, rankings ordered by score.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section id="faq">
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<details><summary>Can a provider pay for the #1 spot?</summary><p>No. Rankings are ordered by score, and payment never changes a score or a ranking position.</p></details>
<details><summary>How often do you update reviews?</summary><p>We aim to re-check each review every 90 days. The "Last verified" date on each page shows when that last happened.</p></details>
<details><summary>Who funds BeVerified?</summary><p>Affiliate commissions from some provider sign-ups. See How we make money above.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can a provider correct its review?</summary><p>Yes, with a source we can check. Accepted corrections update the facts; the score only moves if the rubric says it should.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does a high score mean a provider is compliant for my business?</summary><p>No. A score reflects our rubric, not a legal opinion. Do your own due diligence before signing a contract.</p></details>
</section>

